# 13. SHARED UI AND SETTINGS

Use one shared application layout for Core and future Modules.

The layout may include header, sidebar, breadcrumb, content area and responsive navigation.

Navigation metadata must be registered and permission-filtered.

The backend remains the security boundary.

Define central design tokens for colors, typography, spacing, borders, radii and breakpoints.

Provide accessible focus states, labels, contrast and keyboard behavior.

Reusable components may include buttons, inputs, selects, tables, pagination, alerts, modals, empty states and loading states.

Forms require server-side validation.

Client-side validation is usability support only.

State-changing browser forms require CSRF protection.

Settings must distinguish organization-wide system settings from personal user preferences.

Sensitive settings must be masked.

Settings have types, validation, defaults, ownership and audit rules.

Branding settings must not alter security policy.

Maintenance mode must provide a safe response to browser and API callers.

