# 14. INTERNAL API — FUTURE MODULE COMMUNICATION

The Internal API is an in-process PHP service contract. It is not automatically public HTTP.

Future Modules use registered action names and documented service interfaces.

Each action declares unique name, owner, purpose, input schema, output schema, permission, read/write behavior and error codes.

Duplicate action names fail registration.

Unknown actions are rejected.

Never include a PHP file based on an untrusted action string.

The caller context must be trusted and immutable during the call.

Validate all inputs even when the caller is another Module.

Return a documented result structure.

Do not return raw SQL errors or private exception details.

Cross-Module data access must use the owning Module's API, not private table queries.

Each action needs success, invalid-input, forbidden, not-found, conflict and failure tests as applicable.

