# 27. IMPLEMENTATION ROADMAP

**Phase 0 — Audit:** Read documentation, inspect repository, verify runtime, extensions, Git and existing files.

**Phase 1 — Skeleton:** Reconcile folders, create public entry point, bootstrap, configuration, logger, error handler, Request, Response and Router.

**Phase 2 — Database:** Central PDO manager, Core schema, migration runner, integrity checks, backup and restore tests.

**Phase 3 — Authentication:** First administrator, login, logout, password hashing, session security, account status and throttling.

**Phase 4 — User/RBAC:** User CRUD, roles, permissions, assignment, authorization service and audit.

**Phase 5 — UI:** Shared layout, design tokens, responsive components, user screens, settings and navigation.

**Phase 6 — Internal API:** Registry, caller context, validation, output contracts and tests.

**Phase 7 — External API:** Versioned gateway, client registry, token hashing, scopes, rate limits, pagination, JSON contract and documentation.

**Phase 8 — Operations:** Diagnostics, maintenance mode, backup, restore, logs and deployment guide.

**Phase 9 — Acceptance:** Automated tests, browser tests, security review, API tests, restore test, documentation review and handover.

No business Module begins until Core acceptance is verified.

