# 30. FINAL ARCHITECTURE RULE — FUTURE MODULE INDEPENDENCE

The Core provides shared infrastructure only.

Each future Module has a different business purpose and may have a different workflow, data model, screens, status lifecycle, approvals, reports and rules.

Do not force all Modules into one generic CRUD workflow.

Each Module owns its business logic and its table namespace.

Each Module uses the central database connection.

Each Module communicates with another Module through documented Internal APIs.

Each Module may expose approved resources through the External API after security and data-exposure review.

No Module may query another Module's private tables directly.

The Core must not assume that every Module has the same schema.

External applications must consume approved versioned API resources, never direct database access.

The Core must be built and verified first. Only then should the 50 Modules be designed and developed one by one.

